module athanor_pcscd_cgroup 1.0;

require {
    type pcscd_t;
    type cgroup_t;
    class dir { getattr search open };
}

# pcscd searches the root of the cgroup2 tree once for every client that connects to
# /run/pcscd/pcscd.comm: one `opensc-tool -l` gives one denial, and a session client that
# polls the reader list gives one every five minutes (#509). Fedora's policy denies it in
# selinux-policy-targeted 43.10, and upstream grants it as fs_search_cgroup_dirs(pcscd_t)
# (fedora-selinux/selinux-policy aaf559c0 "Allow pcscd_t to search cgroup", on rawhide
# only, in no 43.x release as of 2026-10-16). This is that interface's cgroup_t rule; its
# two others are not needed: pcscd_t already reads sysfs, and the tmpfs search serves the
# cgroup v1 layout, which the image does not mount. Search lets pcscd resolve paths in
# the cgroup tree, not read the files there, and pcscd.service mounts the tree read-only
# (ProtectControlGroups=yes).
#
# Drop this module once the Fedora release the image is built on ships aaf559c0.
allow pcscd_t cgroup_t:dir { getattr search open };
